   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Dettato \u2014 Separate to MIDI (Roformer 6-stem)\n\nFull separation-to-MIDI chain: **Load Audio \u2192 Roformer Separate** (the `sw-6stem` checkpoint: bass / drums / other / vocals / guitar / piano) **\u2192 six \u00d7 Roformer To Audio \u2192 Dettato Transcribe to MIDI \u2192 Save MIDI + Piano Roll**.\n\n- Each stem gets one **Roformer To Audio** node (the `stem` dropdown is narrowed to the model's six stems once the Separate node is connected); the six AUDIO outputs fill the Transcribe slots `audio_0`\u2026`audio_5` in any order you like.\n- The Dettato chain is **Loader \u2192 Evidence \u2192 Grouper \u2192 Drums**: a stage node not in the graph is bypassed, and its weights are never downloaded. The drums stage needs a 40 kHz or faster source \u2014 the separator's 44.1 kHz stems qualify.\n- Each source runs the full chain, its tracks merge in slot order (name collisions get 'Name (audio_N)'), and one General MIDI file is written \u2014 drum tracks included when the Drums stage is attached.\n- **Transcribe's `dedup` toggle is ON in this workflow**: when the same instrument was transcribed from several stems, only the stem with the most notes of it is kept before the merge, so no duplicate 'Drums (audio_N)' / 'Piano (audio_N)' tracks survive. For sources that are different recordings, turn it off.\n- The output is performance MIDI; if you want the notes to sit on the grid, run the `midi` output through a **Dettato Quantize MIDI** node (not in this graph) with the song's `tempo` and `grid`.\n- **Piano Roll** renders one lane per track (drums in the lower panel)"
   ]
  },
